This is the Alter et al. (2007) disfluency study using the Cognitive Reflection Test (CRT) in a hard-to-read font. The original had N=41 and p just under .05. Many-labs-style replications, including Thompson et al. (2013), failed to find the effect, and a meta-analysis found little evidence for a disfluency benefit on CRT-type reasoning. This specific claim was probably tested in a replication project, possibly Many Labs 1 or the Social Sciences Replication Project, and it is likely to have failed. The original is a small-sample, borderline-significant result with a large implausible effect size.

I recognize the study, and I recall that replications of the disfluency effect mostly failed.

